        </p>
        <ContactForm client:visible />
      </div>
    </Section>

    <!-- Section: Lokasi (R5, page 5). The map banner was MOVED here from
         LayananSection.astro (spec §3, S5 row 2 and roadmap L3.8) — the page had
         one map, in the wrong section, and duplicating it would mean two copies of
         one address to keep in sync. What moved is the banner itself, address and
         link together, so the "Buka Google Maps" button is the same element the
         visitor could already reach inside the services panel. -->
    <Section id="lokasi" labelledBy="lokasi-title" class="section-alt border border-line/30 rounded-panel" enter="rise">
      <SectionTitle
        titleKey="profile.loc_title"
        title="Lokasi Kami"
        descKey="profile.loc_desc"
        desc="Kantor kami di Kabupaten Ponorogo, Jawa Timur."
        accent="jobs"
        headingId="lokasi-title"
      />
      {/* Location banner illustration. Decorative, so `alt=""` + aria-hidden:
          the section already states the location in its h2 and its address, and
          the drawing is a skyline band with no unique information in it.

          `aspect-[2/1]` matches the file's 1200x600 exactly, so the ratio is
          reserved before load and the section does not jump. Rounding is on the
          wrapper (`rounded-panel overflow-hidden`) so the corners clip the
          image, rather than relying on the image's own corners.

          `loading="lazy"` here — unlike the hero, this band is far below the
          fold and is never the LCP element. */}
      <picture class="u-drift-frame block mt-6 aspect-[2/1] overflow-clip rounded-panel border border-line/30">
        <source
          type="image/avif"
          srcset="/assets/ilustrasi/lokasi-banner.avif 1x, /assets/ilustrasi/lokasi-banner@2x.avif 2x"
        />
        <source
          type="image/webp"
          srcset="/assets/ilustrasi/lokasi-banner.webp 1x, /assets/ilustrasi/lokasi-banner@2x.webp 2x"
        />
        <img
          src="/assets/ilustrasi/lokasi-banner.webp"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          width="1200"
          height="600"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="u-drift"
        />
      </picture>
      <div class="u-surface-depth mt-8 bg-surface-raised border border-line rounded-panel p-5 md:p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between items-center gap-5 text-center sm:text-left">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-red-900/30 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <Icon name="map-marker-alt" class="text-red-500 text-xl" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-white font-bold text-body-sm mb-1" data-lang="landing.maps_title">
              Kunjungi LPK Amanah Sakura Japan
            </p>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-fg-muted max-w-xl" data-lang={CONTACT_ADDRESS.key}>
              {CONTACT_ADDRESS.text}
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a
          id="maps-lpk-link"
          href={CONTACT_MAPS_URL}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="u-lift inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-control bg-surface border border-line text-fg text-body-sm font-bold transition whitespace-nowrap"
          style="--u-glow: var(--color-accent-sky);"
        >
          <Icon name="location-arrow" />
          <span data-lang="profile.loc_open_maps">Buka di Google Maps</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </Section>
  </main>

  <!-- ─── Pita dekoratif Jepang (asanoha) ──────────────────────────────
       The ONE landingside gamefeel element that needs no visitor state.

       WHY THIS IS A BARE BAND AND NOT A LAYER INSIDE A Section. `Section`
       renders `py-14 md:py-20` with no `relative`, so an absolutely-positioned
       child would escape its box and paint over the section above it. A band
       with its own `relative` + `overflow-hidden` is self-contained: it cannot
       bleed, and it cannot cover content it does not own.

       WHY IT CARRIES NO TEXT AND NO HEADING. `e2e/test-headings.mjs` asserts
       `/` has EXACTLY ONE h1, and the L2 work already had to move that h1 into
       the hero. A decorative band that also announced itself would be the
       second heading on the page. `JapanTexture` renders none, and its suite
       fails if that changes.

       WHY NOTHING IS SCORED HERE. A visitor has no account, so any number on
       this page would be invented — docs/ILLUSTRATION_SPEC.md §6.0 calls that
       out as reading as surveillance rather than game. There are no numbers,
       no levels and no badges in this band, deliberately. -->
  <!-- Gradient accent divider — replaces the asanoha texture band.
       The old JapanTexture band was purely decorative and loaded a complex SVG
       pattern. The gradient accent line is simpler, theme-responsive (via
       --accent-line in theme.css), and echoes the footer's top divider for
       visual consistency. -->
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 my-8">
    <div class="accent-line w-full rounded-full"></div>
  </div>

  <ClosingBand />
</BaseLayout>
